    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d697">

                <pb facs="0927" n="813" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg813"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">550.E1/295: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Child</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Genoa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-19T14:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 19, 1922—2
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 19—11:03
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>64. Plenary session ending Genoa Conference was perfunctory. Lloyd George rebuked
                    Soviet delegates for their memorandum of May 11,<anchor n="34" xml:id="d697-f1"
                    /> as he had indicated to me that he would.</p>
                <p>I will reach Rome May 22.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Child</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
